  "articleBody": "It's a common scenario: you've acquired a foreclosed property, and beneath the surface, there's more damage than you initially saw. Don't panic! The key here is a methodical approach. First, understand that foreclosures often sit vacant or neglected, making concealed issues like leaks, electrical problems, or even structural wear a real possibility. Your best bet is to conduct a thorough inspection of utilities and moisture. Check every system—plumbing, electrical, and HVAC—to confirm its status before you even think about cosmetic repairs. Prioritize structural work first, then systems, followed by insulation and moisture control. Only after these critical elements are sound should you move onto things like drywall and finishes. Trying to skip ahead and patch things up cosmetically without addressing the root cause will almost always lead to bigger, more expensive problems down the line. If you're unsure about the extent of hidden damage or feel overwhelmed, that's definitely a sign it's time to bring in experienced professionals like us at HH Remodeling LLC. We can help you identify and address these issues correctly from the start.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}